_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.08355236236201896,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":3,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":33.3,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.12586123350602874,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":90.3,"_gate_rev_durability":0.16402487307364577,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.04128408810382892,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":57.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.04927671649878573,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.015042193909098035,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":74.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.031489998,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":21.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.333,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":33.3,"pf":[],"description_full":"Peoples Bancorp Inc. operates as the financial holding company for Peoples Bank that provides commercial and consumer banking products and services. The company accepts various deposit products, including demand deposit accounts, savings accounts, money market accounts, certificates of deposit, and governmental deposits; and provides commercial and industrial, commercial real estate, construction, finance, residential real estate, and consumer indirect and direct loans, as well as home equity lines of credit and overdrafts. It also offers debit and automated teller machine (ATM) cards; safe deposit rental facilities; money orders and cashier's checks; and online, telephone, and mobile banking services. In addition, it provides various life, health, and property and casualty insurance products; third-party insurance administration; interactive teller machines; insurance premium financing; commercial and technology equipment leasing; fiduciary and trust; equipment financing agreements; and asset management and administration services, as well as employee benefit, retirement, and healthcare plan administration services. Further, the company offers brokerage services through an unaffiliated registered broker-dealer; and credit cards to individuals and businesses, as well as merchant credit card transaction processing, and person-to-person and business-to-business payment processing services. Peoples Bancorp Inc. was founded in 1902 and is based in Marietta, Ohio.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Tyler J. Wilcox | President, CEO & Director | Age 47 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $314K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 16%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $88K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Peoples Bancorp Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.4B market cap on $459M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years and +16% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $129M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 28 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.26\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 0.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 3.1% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 22% margin of safety against estimated fair value","33 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Responsive Playbooks and the PEBO Inflection","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/8/Responsive_Playbooks_and_the_PEBO_Inflection_110326121202_1793682722.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793682722.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.612,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What Is Drawing Fresh Attention To Peoples Bancorp (PEBO)?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-pebo/peoples-bancorp/news/what-is-drawing-fresh-attention-to-peoples-bancorp-pebo","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793583024.114,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.784,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Why Is Peoples Bancorp (NASDAQ:PEBO) Gaining Market Attention Now?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/financial/why-is-peoples-bancorp-nasdaqpebo-gaining-market-attention-now","date":"2026-11-01","timestamp":1793534280.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.715,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Peoples Bancorp of North Carolina (NASDAQ:PEBK) & Bank Of Montreal (NYSE:BMO) Head to Head Comparison","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/peoples-bancorp-of-north-carolina-nasdaqpebk-bank-of-montreal-nysebmo-head-to-head-comparison.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793895343.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.924,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Don't Ignore The Insider Selling In Peoples Bancorp of North Carolina","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-pebk/peoples-bancorp-of-north-carolina/news/dont-ignore-the-insider-selling-in-peoples-bancorp-of-north-3","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793786423.074,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.587,"tier":1,"scope":"compa